<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trier</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Trier is a city in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moselle">Moselle</a> River, founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> and one of the oldest cities in Germany. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> its archbishop was one of the leading ecclesiastical princes. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-1356">Golden Bull of 1356</a> named the archbishop of Trier as one of the seven <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> who chose the emperor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/trier.jpg" alt="Trier" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CTHOE · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Trier-Blick-vom_Weishaus.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
